from pathlib import Path
import json,html,shutil
O=Path('outputs/30a_finish');v=json.loads((O/'verification.json').read_text());ds=json.loads(Path('work/30a_finish/source/districts.json').read_text());e=html.escape
styles='body{margin:0;background:#f5f1e6;color:#29453c;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:40px}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia}h1{font-size:46px}h2{margin-top:48px}a{color:#ad4d23}img{width:100%;display:block;border-radius:8px}section{margin:30px 0}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}figure{margin:0}figcaption{padding:12px 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #d4d9ca}.note{padding:20px;background:#e5e9d9;border-radius:10px}.pending{background:#f2debe}code{background:#e2e7da;padding:2px 5px}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:18px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}'
s=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>30A — evidence and review</title><style>'+styles+'</style><main><small>FLORIDA COASTAL · OCTOBER 16, 2026</small><h1>30A: evidence and review</h1><p>A rebuilt geographic base and neighborhood study. This is a review candidate, not a claim that every acceptance gate has passed.</p><p><a href="../../../explore_coast.html?view=30a&level=region">Open the map</a> · <a href="assets/30a-finished.glb">Download genuine 3D GLB</a> · <a href="verification.json">Machine-readable checks</a> · <a href="alignment.csv">Alignment measurements</a></p>']
s+=['<div class="note"><b>Measured:</b> 12 district anchors on land; 15 named lake polygons; maximum final-GLB lake boundary displacement '+str(v['maxActualGlbLakeErrorMeters'])+' m from OSM; '+f"{v['glbBytes']/1e6:.2f}"+' MB uncompressed GLB; '+f"{v['coldRegionBytes']/1e6:.2f}"+' MB regional cold-load file budget. This budget includes the shared viewer and data, excluding HTTP overhead.</div>','<div class="note pending"><b>Still open:</b> physical mid-range-phone cold-load test; blind recognition by a local; measured heights for most buildings; surveyed tree density. Pricing is a checked sample of asking-price examples, not an exhaustive or representative market range. Other regions retain legacy geometry and scale until this candidate is accepted.</div>']
s+=['<h2>Before / after</h2><p>Unedited browser captures, same desktop viewport. State and Region retain their comparison role. Town now shows a 1.25 km neighborhood instead of the former broad town framing; the changed camera scale is intentional.</p>']
for level in ['state','region','town']:
 s.append('<section><h3>'+level.title()+'</h3><div class="pair"><figure><img src="before/'+level+'.png"><figcaption>Before</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="after/'+level+'.png"><figcaption>After</figcaption></figure></div></section>')
s+=['<h2>Geographic evidence</h2><p>The overlay uses actual OpenStreetMap tiles. Lake error is the maximum Hausdorff distance between boundary edges extracted from the exported GLB triangles and the source OSM polygon. Town error compares the actual viewer anchor with its source place node. These are same-source fidelity measurements, not independent survey accuracy. OSM place nodes are locality labels, not legal district centroids. Existing 100 m atlas land supplies surrounding context outside the rebuilt extent.</p><a href="osm-overlay.png"><img src="osm-overlay.png" alt="Model shorelines and town anchors over OpenStreetMap, with measured errors"></a><table><tr><th>Place</th><th>Measurement</th><th>Error</th><th>Source</th></tr>']
for r in v['rows']:s.append(f'<tr><td>{e(r["name"])}</td><td>{e(r["kind"])}</td><td>{r["error_m"]:.3f} m</td><td><a href="{e(r["source"])}">OSM geometry</a></td></tr>')
s+=['</table><h2>The rule book</h2><ol><li><b>Geography first.</b> Preserve vector coastline, bay holes and lake topology. Never substitute raster silhouettes. Compare exported geometry with the original source after compression.</li><li><b>One scale rule.</b> <code>height = min(realHeight × multiplier, shorterFootprintSide × 3)</code>; buildings multiplier 3, trees 5. Roof counts toward the limit. The authoritative constant is <a href="scale-rule.json">scale-rule.json</a>. OSM heights/levels take precedence; missing residential levels are explicitly assumed as two, including Alys. Only 15 buildings here have level metadata. The Coleman Pavilion height is an assumption pending measurement.</li><li><b>Neighborhoods follow mapped footprints and streets.</b> Keep Seaside porch cottages, Rosemary masonry townhouses, Alys white courtyards and WaterColor lowcountry roofs distinct. Actual facades are stylized, not individually surveyed replicas. Small footprints are inset to reduce overlap.</li><li><b>Canopy follows evidence.</b> Point Washington forest uses OSM relation 11982445 plus mapped woods, with softened edges. Town vegetation placement uses classified aerial imagery. An 8 m candidate spacing and varied crowns are illustration assumptions, not verified stem density. No invented forest census.</li><li><b>Three deliberate scales.</b> State for orientation; Region for the 30-mile comparison; Town for neighborhood detail at 45° camera tilt. Labels keep their source anchors. Phone labels thin out, while every district remains in the selector.</li><li><b>Source every decision.</b> Each district retains its place guide, OSM anchor, checked asking-price examples and source URLs. Lake taps open their mapped shoreline source. Bay ramps and marinas remain in the bay; walkability follows the mapped Timpoochee Trail; ECP routes use road geometry and no-live-traffic time estimates.</li><li><b>Gate before propagation.</b> Repeat export-error, file-size, console, phone and blind-recognition checks before treating this as the template for another region. No new catalog regions were added.</li></ol>']
s+=['<h2>Price evidence</h2><p>Checked October 16, 2026. Residential asking-price examples; land, fractional interests and obvious commercial/multi-home packages excluded. Source search boundaries can differ from neighborhood boundaries. Santa Rosa Beach means the coastal Gulf Place area here, not the entire postal area. Inlet Beach uses two independently checked listing examples. Open the evidence JSON for listing IDs, subdivisions and source pages.</p><p><a href="district-price-evidence.json">Download district evidence</a></p><table><tr><th>District</th><th>Observed examples</th><th>Place guide</th><th>Price source</th></tr>']
for d in ds:s.append(f'<tr><td>{e(d["name"])}</td><td>${d["priceEvidence"]["min"]:,.0f}–${d["priceEvidence"]["max"]:,.0f}</td><td><a href="{e(d["source"])}">Guide</a></td><td><a href="{e(d["priceSource"])}">Listings</a></td></tr>')
s+=['</table><h2>Blind district review</h2><p>Have a local name each crop before opening its answer. This test has not been passed merely by producing these images. The same camera scale is used for all crops; some adjacent districts share architectural vocabulary.</p><div class="pair">']
for i,d in enumerate(ds,1):s.append(f'<figure><img src="crops/{i:02d}.png" alt="Unlabeled district crop {i}"><figcaption>Crop {i:02d}<details><summary>Reveal district</summary>{e(d["name"])}</details></figcaption></figure>')
s+=['</div><h2>Runtime checks</h2><p>The 390 × 844 responsive layout was checked on desktop hardware. Observed local load was approximately 0.6 seconds; that is not a phone performance benchmark. Direct Western Lake selection, lake menu, priority layers and regional town filtering were exercised. No application console errors were observed in the candidate during these checks. See <a href="browser-checks.json">recorded browser checks</a>.</p><h2>Reference trail</h2><ul>']
for url,label in [('https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/11982445','Point Washington State Forest'),('https://www.visitsouthwalton.com/blog/a-guide-to-the-timpoochee-trail/','Timpoochee Trail'),('https://www.visitsouthwalton.com/blog/coastal-dune-lakes/','Coastal dune lakes'),('https://alysbeach.com/architecture-and-design/','Alys architecture'),('https://rosemarybeach.com/explore-rosemary-beach/architecture-design/','Rosemary architecture'),('https://www.corgan.com/projects/watercolor-beach-club','WaterColor architectural reference'),('https://seasidefl.com/news/a-walk-through-seaside/','Seaside pavilion reference'),('https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer','Aerial reference service')]:s.append(f'<li><a href="{url}">{label}</a></li>')
s+=['</ul><p>© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL. Aerial-derived canopy: Esri, Vantor, Earthstar Geographics and the GIS User Community. Aerial imagery interpretation is approximate; acquisition dates vary.</p></main></html>']
(O/'index.html').write_text(''.join(s));shutil.copy2('work/30a_finish/scale-rule.json',O/'scale-rule.json');shutil.copy2('work/30a_finish/source/districts.json',O/'district-price-evidence.json')
